From 465808236a547bdffc45c05f3935c0e2249ead99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:31:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mantle's BOM: lead-free brass, the Rega kit at $265, the
 laminated plinth (round 43)

- fabkit: a 'brass-leadfree' material (C69300 Eco Brass or C27450) beside 'brass' (C360), so other products keep theirs
- platter-hub, bearing-housing, pod-core in lead-free brass (certification.md, R3), their notes to match
- components.json rega-24v-motor: $265, Audio Advisor (mantle-drive.md)
- the plinth and platter: a prototype note, two 1/2 in TruCast sheets laminated and machined to 25.4 (stock-colours.md);
  the drawn 25 unchanged
- rebuilt: the budget $3,815 to $3,910 (the motor +$65, the brass +$30); 0 clashes; the DXFs unchanged but for
  their timestamps, so left out

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VCPNDaozJgar2mVTSvis3A
